**How to implement.** The constructor windows compose the real Send kit… and Copy experiments… seams (the S6 brief: Send kit… through a save dialog defaulting to the DataLocations exports folder; 001 §G: the suggested parent of kit folders is the kits folder; .spec-md §3.9: every location comes from settings). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `AppContext` gains `locations : DataLocations` (step 81), documented in one line (the locations the app scope was composed over, where its windows' dialogs start), set by `compose` (step 89) from its `locations` argument, so `create` and `recreateLibrary` carry it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (step 189): the shell is `{ KitWindowShell.inert with explorer = ExplorerProxy.system; requestClose = window.Close; zipPicker = KitZipPicker.ofWindow window context.locations.exportsFolder; archive = KitArchiveProxy.create (); archiveJobs = KitArchiveJobHost.onUiThread (fun p -> dispatch (SendKitProgressed p)) (fun r -> dispatch (SendKitEnded r)); kitPicker = KitFolderPicker.ofWindow window context.locations.kitsFolder }` (steps 150, 199, 200, 201, 225), over the dispatch the mount captures from its init command; `mount` takes the `AppContext` for it, which `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` pass. Their docs say, in no more words, that the kit bar sends and copies through the real dialogs. No other seam changes. Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `the app scope carries the locations it was composed over`: `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "AppContextTests")` holds `locations` equal to `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName "AppContextTests")` (step 83). `KitWindowTests` gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `a constructor window's kit bar offers Send kit, and Copy experiments only to a kit opened read-write`: a shown `MainConstructorWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitWindowTests")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152) holds `sendKitButton` and `kitCopyExperimentsButton`; over that kit closed and opened again read-only it holds `sendKitButton` and no `kitCopyExperimentsButton`. Neither is pressed, because a real window's dialogs are the system's (the S5.3 Show in Explorer precedent). The windows' consumers keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the constructor windows are wired, `AppContext.locations` MUST hold the composed locations and the windows' kit shell MUST hold the real save dialog over the exports folder, the real archive and job host and the real kit folder dialog; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `a constructor window's kit bar offers Send kit, and Copy experiments only to a kit opened read-write`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app scope carries the locations it was composed over`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
